# The stall, in a bomber: entering it, recognising it, and getting out of it
# with the least height lost.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The speed is this aeroplane's own.** `stall` is its stall speed in the
# landing configuration. For the aeroplanes in this class that figure is
# **measured from the flight model rather than published** - no flight manual
# for them is public - and the figure itself says so. `docs/ASSETS.md` records
# which aeroplanes those are, and which are left out for having no such figure
# that holds still.
#
# **The stall is approached, not reached.** The entry ends a good margin above
# the stall speed, because what this class of aeroplane does at the stall
# itself is not something a lesson should be flying an aeroplane into: the
# exercise is recognising the approach to it and getting out.
#
# **The stall is entered in the landing configuration**, flaps and gear down,
# because `stall` is the stall with everything down: flown clean, a swept wing
# asked for twenty-five knots above its landing stall has to stall to get
# there, and departs. **The bands are measured**, with room: the B-2A holds its height to within 8 feet entering it and loses 119 in the recovery (53 before 2026-09-26, when the recovery became the autopilot's stall recovery).

name Stalls in a bomber
teaches bomber

stage Entering the stall
do Close the throttles and hold the height as the speed comes back
do Keep the wings level: a wing drop is what you are avoiding
hold position/h-agl-ft start-100 start+100 Hold the height as the speed comes back
until velocities/vc-kts <= stall+25

stage The recovery
do Move the control column forward to unstall the wing
do Full power as the nose comes down, and level the wings
need position/h-agl-ft >= start-300 Recover with the least height you can
until velocities/vc-kts >= stall+35
